    "text": "<p>Ammonia reacts with carbon dioxide and water to form ammonium bicarbonate.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><munder><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Ammonium carbonate reacts with sodium chloride to form sodium bicarbonate and ammonium chloride.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><munder><msub><mi>NaHCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math></p>",
